# A `#FX(…)` cap on a type binds every path its methods run, on every tier: a
# lambda written in a method, a trait default body the type inherits, the
# type's `Close` impl, a function field's fixed row and a call through a
# trait-value field (every implementation counts), each at the method that
# runs it. A method row inside the cap may only tighten it. A type that stays
# inside its cap checks clean, and the cap is erased before IR: the program
# prints the same on every tier.
fixture: type_cap_binds_every_path/input
env: NO_COLOR=1
step: jet check closure.jet
exit: 1
stderr: count "Error [" = 1 # exactly this many
stderr: ~ "`loud` reaches the `IO` effect, which type `Maker` denies" # the lambda's print belongs to the method
step: jet run -O0 closure.jet
exit: 1
stderr: ~ "`loud` reaches the `IO` effect, which type `Maker` denies" # O0 refuses it
step: jet run -O1 closure.jet
exit: 1
stderr: ~ "`loud` reaches the `IO` effect, which type `Maker` denies" # O1 refuses it
step: jet run -O2 closure.jet
exit: 1
stderr: ~ "`loud` reaches the `IO` effect, which type `Maker` denies" # O2 refuses it
step: jet check default.jet
exit: 1
stderr: count "Error [" = 1 # exactly this many
stderr: ~ "`show` reaches the `IO` effect, which type `Square` denies" # the inherited default body is the type's method
stderr: ~ "default.jet:5:5" # reported at the default body
stderr: ~ "type `Square` is capped here" # the cap is the secondary label
step: jet run -O0 default.jet
exit: 1
stderr: ~ "`show` reaches the `IO` effect, which type `Square` denies" # O0 refuses it
step: jet run -O1 default.jet
exit: 1
stderr: ~ "`show` reaches the `IO` effect, which type `Square` denies" # O1 refuses it
step: jet run -O2 default.jet
exit: 1
stderr: ~ "`show` reaches the `IO` effect, which type `Square` denies" # O2 refuses it
step: jet check close.jet
exit: 1
stderr: count "Error [" = 1 # exactly this many
stderr: ~ "`close` reaches the `IO` effect, which type `Handle` denies" # the Close impl is bound
step: jet run -O0 close.jet
exit: 1
stderr: ~ "`close` reaches the `IO` effect, which type `Handle` denies" # O0 refuses it
step: jet run -O1 close.jet
exit: 1
stderr: ~ "`close` reaches the `IO` effect, which type `Handle` denies" # O1 refuses it
step: jet run -O2 close.jet
exit: 1
stderr: ~ "`close` reaches the `IO` effect, which type `Handle` denies" # O2 refuses it
step: jet check field.jet
exit: 1
stderr: count "Error [" = 2 # the field and the method that calls it
stderr: ~ "`go` reaches the `IO` effect, which type `Holder` denies" # the field's fixed row counts at the call
stderr: ~ "[jet.TypeFieldCapExceeded]: Field `act`'s row declares `IO`, which type `Holder` doesn't allow" # the field path has its own code
step: jet run -O0 field.jet
exit: 1
stderr: ~ "`go` reaches the `IO` effect, which type `Holder` denies" # O0 refuses it
step: jet run -O1 field.jet
exit: 1
stderr: ~ "`go` reaches the `IO` effect, which type `Holder` denies" # O1 refuses it
step: jet run -O2 field.jet
exit: 1
stderr: ~ "`go` reaches the `IO` effect, which type `Holder` denies" # O2 refuses it
step: jet check trait_field.jet
exit: 1
stderr: count "Error [" = 1 # exactly this many
stderr: ~ "`show` reaches the `FS.Read` effect, which type `Report` denies" # the trait-value field brings Disk's read
step: jet run -O0 trait_field.jet
exit: 1
stderr: ~ "`show` reaches the `FS.Read` effect, which type `Report` denies" # O0 refuses it
step: jet run -O1 trait_field.jet
exit: 1
stderr: ~ "`show` reaches the `FS.Read` effect, which type `Report` denies" # O1 refuses it
step: jet run -O2 trait_field.jet
exit: 1
stderr: ~ "`show` reaches the `FS.Read` effect, which type `Report` denies" # O2 refuses it
step: jet check row.jet
exit: 1
stderr: count "Error [" = 1 # exactly this many
stderr: ~ "`say` reaches the `IO` effect, which type `Logger` denies" # a row can't widen the cap
step: jet run -O0 row.jet
exit: 1
stderr: ~ "`say` reaches the `IO` effect, which type `Logger` denies" # O0 refuses it
step: jet run -O1 row.jet
exit: 1
stderr: ~ "`say` reaches the `IO` effect, which type `Logger` denies" # O1 refuses it
step: jet run -O2 row.jet
exit: 1
stderr: ~ "`say` reaches the `IO` effect, which type `Logger` denies" # O2 refuses it
step: jet check within.jet
exit: 0
step: jet run -O0 within.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "181\n"
step: jet run -O1 within.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "181\n"
step: jet run -O2 within.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "181\n"
